my-shop namespace. Maybe I should first use kubectl to get the services in that namespace. But the available tools include exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd. So perhaps I should use that to run \'kubectl get services -n astronomy-shop\' to get the list. \n\nWait, but the user\'s initial step was to use get_services. Maybe the get_services tool is designed to get services from Grafana, which might be a different source. But the user\'s application is in a specific namespace. This is a bit confusing. However, the user\'s first step was to use get_services, so maybe I should proceed with that. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the get_services tool is part of the monitoring stack and returns services that are being monitored. But without more info, I have to follow the user\'s initial choice. So the correct tool call is get_services with no arguments. \n\nSo the tool call would be:\n\n{"name": "get_services", "arguments": {}}\n\nThat\'s the correct step here. Once I have the list of services, I can then check each one\'s metrics, dependencies, and logs. But for now, the first step is to get the services.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{}', 'name': 'get_services'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-af8fc05528a1c7b4', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 852, 'prompt_tokens': 2473, 'total_tokens': 3325, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb57-2431-77e0-9348-b224fe78a64a-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'get_services', 'args': {}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-af8fc05528a1c7b4', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2473, 'output_tokens': 852, 'total_tokens': 3325}), ToolMessage(content='meta=None content=[TextContent(type=\'text\', text="[\'frontend-proxy\', 