ify specific faults by examining trace data for services with high call counts (e.g., `load-generator` or `frontend-proxy`). This will reveal errors, latency spikes, or failed requests that could indicate root causes such as misconfigurations, resource exhaustion, or faulty logic in the microservices. Focusing on high-traffic services ensures we prioritize areas most likely to impact system behavior.", additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=453, prompt_tokens=2189, total_tokens=2642, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb57-7aa7-7993-9708-910ec869d53e-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2189, 'output_tokens': 453, 'total_tokens': 2642}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='21a2e674-3acc-456e-bc6a-4c0eb65c7369')]]
