es for the services involved in those calls. The load-generator service has a lot of calls to frontend-proxy, so checking the traces for load-generator or frontend-proxy would be a good start. Alternatively, the frontend-proxy is called by many others, so its traces might show issues propagating through the system.\n\nThe get_traces function requires a service name and a time range. Since the previous dependency graph used a 5-minute window, it's consistent to use the same time frame here. The user should pick a service that's part of the high call counts. Let's go with 'frontend-proxy' because it's a central service in the dependency graph, being called by load-generator and calling frontend. Checking its traces could reveal if there are errors or latency issues in the service, which might be causing faults in the application. So, the tool call would be get_traces with service 'frontend-proxy' and last_n_minutes 5.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"service": "frontend-proxy", "last_n_minutes": 5}', 'name': 'get_traces'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-ab9e97b982c7e62a', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 375, 'prompt_tokens': 3184, 'total_tokens': 3559, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb57-8fe9-75b0-9089-51232005360b-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'get_traces', 'args': {'service': 'frontend-proxy', 'last_n_minutes': 5}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-ab9e97b982c7e62a', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3184, 'output_tokens': 375, 'total_tokens': 3559}), ToolMessage(content="[{'traceID': '6e6d768c7614b9d99c145967721eac92', 'spans': [{'traceID': '6e6d768c7614b9d99c145967721eac92', 'spanID': '49bbc762ab9e6e6a', 'operationName': 