nect to `valkey-cart:6379`. This suggests a dependency issue: either the `valkey-cart` service is not running, misconfigured, or unreachable.  \n\n**Command**: `kubectl get pods -n astronomy-shop -l app.kubernetes.io/name=valkey-cart`  \n**Reason**: Verify if the `valkey-cart` pods are running and healthy. If no pods are available or they are crashing, this would directly explain why the `cart` service cannot connect to Redis.  \n\n**Follow-up Command**: `kubectl get endpoints -n astronomy-shop valkey-cart`  \n**Reason**: Confirm if the `valkey-cart` service has valid endpoints (i.e., pods assigned to it). Empty endpoints would mean no pods are available to accept connections.", additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 525, 'prompt_tokens': 14113, 'total_tokens': 14638, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb59-1889-77d2-beb1-26b2b7b5a114-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 14113, 'output_tokens': 525, 'total_tokens': 14638}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='73b008bf-9c91-4bc8-8ec1-1ea6b9e8e419'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is trying to figure out why the cart service in the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop is failing. From the previous steps, they found that the cart container is crashing with a segmentation fault, and the logs point to a connection issue with valkey-cart:6379. \n\nSo, the next logical step is to check the valkey-cart service. The user mentioned using kubectl to get pods labeled with app.kubernetes.io/name=valkey-cart. That makes sense because if those pods aren't running, the cart service can't connect to Redis. \n\nWait, the 